 - **ProviderRegistry** — registers all available providers
 - **FailoverManager** — automatic failover between providers on error
 - **ModelDiscovery** — detects available models across providers
-- **UnifiedModelCatalogService** — the authoritative available-model surface for desktop and mobile pickers. It merges static provider defaults, models.dev enrichment, local/remote catalog overrides, user custom models, and CLI-discovered models; stale stored selections are resolved lazily to provider defaults with a visible session note. `npm run sync:model-catalog` refreshes the committed models.dev offline snapshot for pricing/context metadata and offline safety. The scheduled `model-catalog-watch.yml` workflow runs that refresh every six hours, opens or updates one durable issue with the exact diff, and fails on drift so catalogue changes cannot disappear as a transient CI warning. It remains unnecessary for a newly available model to appear when the CLI, custom-model, or override sources report it.
+- **UnifiedModelCatalogService** — the authoritative available-model surface for desktop and mobile pickers. It merges static provider defaults, models.dev enrichment, local/remote catalog overrides, user custom models, and CLI-discovered models; stale stored selections are resolved lazily to provider defaults with a visible session note. `npm run sync:model-catalog` refreshes the committed models.dev offline snapshot for pricing/context metadata and offline safety. The scheduled `model-catalog-watch.yml` workflow runs that refresh every six hours, opens or updates one durable issue carrying the sync instructions and the exact snapshot diff (truncated with a pointer to the job summary when it is too large for an issue). The run stays green on drift because a permanently red run was ignored; the issue is the signal. It goes red only on real errors: models.dev unreachable or empty, install failure, or a GitHub API failure. It remains unnecessary for a newly available model to appear when the CLI, custom-model, or override sources report it.
 - **Model replacements** — `PROVIDER_MODEL_REPLACEMENTS` records deliberate, provider-scoped migrations; AIO never infers them from names or release dates. Persisted automation definitions, defaults, favourites, run snapshots, and history retain their original IDs for auditability, while automation spawn, local/remote instance creation, runtime changes, and general alias normalization resolve replacement chains lazily before catalogue validation. This keeps existing scheduled work executable when AIO retires an old model ID.
 - Providers: Anthropic API (direct), Claude CLI, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI
 
